cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  SDP-Complexity-Study: code and results for "Does Added Complexity Pay Off?"
message: >-
  If you use this software or its results, please cite both the software and
  the paper it accompanies.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Yi
    family-names: Liu
    affiliation: University of Glasgow
    orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0009-0005-3847-3705'
license: MIT
repository-code: 'https://github.com/liuyi200106/SDP-Complexity-Study'
abstract: >-
  Component-wise empirical study of feature selection, resampling and ensembling
  for imbalanced software defect prediction. Measures the marginal contribution
  of each pipeline component across 14 datasets under stratified 5-fold
  cross-validation, with per-fold results and all significance tests published
  alongside the code.
keywords:
  - software defect prediction
  - class imbalance
  - component-wise ablation
  - controlled experiments
  - SHAP
  - feature selection
  - ensemble learning
  - reproducibility

preferred-citation:
  type: article
  title: >-
    Does Added Complexity Pay Off? A Component-Wise Empirical Study of Feature
    Selection, Resampling and Ensembling for Imbalanced Software Defect
    Prediction
  authors:
    - given-names: Yi
      family-names: Liu
      affiliation: University of Glasgow
